2025-12-07 11:20:29,391 - src.api.utils.api_logging - INFO - API_CALL_SUCCESS | Endpoint: get_session_messages | User: ANONYMOUS | Status: 200 | Duration: 1.371s | Response: ["id=23 session_id=6 user_id=1 role='user' content='Explain the concept of Transformers' created_at='2025-12-07T05:16:23.737745+00:00'", "id=24 session_id=6 user_id=1 role='assistant' content='The Transformer is a model architecture that utilizes stacked self-attention and point-wise, fully connected layers for both its encoder and decoder [Figure 1]. It employs a residual connection around each of its two sub-layers, followed by layer normalization [10, 1]. The output of each sub-layer is LayerNorm(x+ Sublayer(x)) [1]. This architecture reduces the number of operations for learning dependencies between distant positions to a constant number, unlike other methods that might be linear or logarithmic [11]. Jakob proposed replacing Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs) with self-attention, and Ashish and Illia designed and implemented the first Transformer models.' created_at='2025-12-07T05:16:33.853097+00:00'"]
