2025-12-07 11:21:23,338 - src.api.utils.api_logging - INFO - API_CALL_SUCCESS | Endpoint: query_documents | User: ANONYMOUS | Status: 200 | Duration: 30.053s | Response: "session_id=6 response={'answer': 'The Transformer architecture heavily relies on self-attention, also known as intra-attention [Attention Is All You Need]. Self-attention is an attention mechanism designed to relate different positions of a single sequence to compute a representation of that sequence [Attention Is All You Need]. The motivation for using self-attention includes considerations for the total computational complexity per layer and the amount of computation [Attention Is All You Need].\\n\\nRegarding attention mechanisms, dot-product attention is noted to be much faster and more space-efficient in practice compared to additive attention, as it can be implemented using highly optimized matrix multiplication code. However, for small values of dk, additive attention can outperform dot-product attention [Attention Is All You Need]. To counteract the effect of averaging attention-weighted positions, Multi-Head Attention is employed [Attention Is All You Need].\\n\\nThe paper \"Attention Is All You Need,\" which introduced the Transformer, lists Ashish Vaswani and Jakob Uszkoreit among its authors [Attention Is All You Need].', 'citations': [{'id': 'test_1.pdf', 'score': 1.251868996493894, 'meta': {'book': 'Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 30', 'date': '2017', 'page': 3, 'type': 'Conference Proceedings', 'title': 'Attention is All you Need', 'author': 'Ashish Vaswani, Noam Shazeer, Niki Parmar, Jakob Uszkoreit, Llion Jones, Aidan N. Gomez, \u0141ukasz Kaiser, Illia Polosukhin', 'source': 'test_1.pdf', 'created': '2017', 'creator': 'PyPDF', 'editors': 'I. Guyon and U.V. Luxburg and S. Bengio and H. Wallach and R. Fergus and S. Vishwanathan and R. Garnett', 'moddate': '2018-02-12T21:22:10-08:00', 'subject': 'Neural Information Processing Systems http://nips.cc/', 'language': 'en-US', 'lastpage': '6008', 'producer': 'PyPDF2', 'eventtype': 'Poster', 'file_name': 'test_1.pdf', 'file_path': 'data\\\\test_1.pdf', 'firstpage': '5998', 'published': '2017', 'publisher': 'Curran Associates, Inc.', 'page_label': '4', 'description': 'Paper accepted and presented at the Neural Information Processing Systems Conference (http://nips.cc/)', 'total_pages': 11, 'creationdate': '', 'file_path_absolute': 'D:\\\\work\\\\RAG\\\\data\\\\test_1.pdf', 'description-abstract': 'The dominant sequence transduction models are based on complex recurrent orconvolutional neural networks in an encoder and decoder configuration. The best performing such models also connect the encoder and decoder through an attentionm echanisms.  We propose a novel, simple network architecture based solely onan attention mechanism, dispensing with recurrence and convolutions entirely.Experiments on two machine translation tasks show these models to be superiorin quality while being more parallelizable and requiring significantly less timeto train. Our single model with 165 million parameters, achieves 27.5 BLEU onEnglish-to-German translation, improving over the existing best ensemble result by over 1 BLEU. On English-to-French translation, we outperform the previoussingle state-of-the-art with model by 0.7 BLEU, achieving a BLEU score of 41.1.'}, 'pdf_file': 'test_1.pdf', 'pdf_path': 'data\\\\test_1.pdf', 'pdf_link': '/api/files/test_1.pdf'}, {'id': 'test_1.pdf', 'score': 1.2573484903603884, 'meta': {'book': 'Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 30', 'date': '2017', 'page': 0, 'type': 'Conference Proceedings', 'title': 'Attention is All you Need', 'author': 'Ashish Vaswani, Noam Shazeer, Niki Parmar, Jakob Uszkoreit, Llion Jones, Aidan N. Gomez, \u0141ukasz Kaiser, Illia Polosukhin', 'source': 'test_1.pdf', 'created': '2017', 'creator': 'PyPDF', 'editors': 'I. Guyon and U.V. Luxburg and S. Bengio and H. Wallach and R. Fergus and S. Vishwanathan and R. Garnett', 'moddate': '2