2025-12-07 11:31:16,298 - src.api.utils.api_logging - INFO - API_CALL_SUCCESS | Endpoint: get_session_messages | User: ANONYMOUS | Status: 200 | Duration: 2.041s | Response: ["id=23 session_id=6 user_id=1 role='user' content='Explain the concept of Transformers' created_at='2025-12-07T05:16:23.737745+00:00'", "id=24 session_id=6 user_id=1 role='assistant' content='The Transformer is a model architecture that utilizes stacked self-attention and point-wise, fully connected layers for both its encoder and decoder [Figure 1]. It employs a residual connection around each of its two sub-layers, followed by layer normalization [10, 1]. The output of each sub-layer is LayerNorm(x+ Sublayer(x)) [1]. This architecture reduces the number of operations for learning dependencies between distant positions to a constant number, unlike other methods that might be linear or logarithmic [11]. Jakob proposed replacing Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs) with self-attention, and Ashish and Illia designed and implemented the first Transformer models.' created_at='2025-12-07T05:16:33.853097+00:00'", "id=33 session_id=6 user_id=1 role='user' content='explain in detail' created_at='2025-12-07T05:50:44.567467+00:00'", "id=34 session_id=6 user_id=1 role='assistant' content='The Transformer architecture heavily relies on self-attention, also known as intra-attention [Attention Is All You Need]. Self-attention is an attention mechanism designed to relate different positions of a single sequence to compute a representation of that sequence [Attention Is All You Need]. The motivation for using self-attention includes considerations for the total computational complexity per layer and the amount of computation [Attention Is All You Need].\\n\\nRegarding attention mechanisms, dot-product attention is noted to be much faster and more space-efficient in practice compared to additive attention, as it can be implemented using highly optimized matrix multiplication code. However, for small values of dk, additive attention can outperform dot-product attention [Attention Is All You Need]. To counteract the effect of averaging attention-weighted positions, Multi-Head Attention is employed [Attention Is All You Need].\\n\\nThe paper \"Attention Is All You Need,\" which introduced the Transformer, lists Ashish Vaswani and Jakob Uszkoreit among its authors [Attention Is All You Need].' created_at='2025-12-07T05:50:55.427518+00:00'"]
