2025-12-07 11:47:03,187 - src.api.utils.api_logging - INFO - API_CALL_SUCCESS | Endpoint: get_session_messages | User: ANONYMOUS | Status: 200 | Duration: 1.123s | Response: ["id=25 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='user' content='what is transformers' citations=None created_at='2025-12-07T05:19:10.677734+00:00'", "id=26 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='assistant' content='The Transformer is a model architecture that uses stacked self-attention and point-wise, fully connected layers for both the encoder and decoder [Figure 1, 3.1]. It is also mentioned in the context of handling problems involving various input and output modalities like text, images, audio, and video [plan to extend the Transformer].' citations=None created_at='2025-12-07T05:19:22.443644+00:00'", "id=27 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='user' content='explain in brief' citations=None created_at='2025-12-07T05:36:03.878968+00:00'", "id=28 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='assistant' content='The Transformer is a model architecture that uses stacked self-attention. Self-attention layers are used for mapping one variable-length sequence of symbol representations to another sequence of equal length, such as in a typical sequence transduction encoder or decoder [4 Why Self-Attention]. An attention function, a core component, maps a query and a set of key-value pairs to an output, which is computed as a weighted sum of the values [3.2 Attention].' citations=None created_at='2025-12-07T05:36:15.578425+00:00'", "id=29 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='user' content='explain layers in transformers' citations=None created_at='2025-12-07T05:38:02.983519+00:00'", "id=30 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='assistant' content='The Transformer architecture uses stacked self-attention and point-wise, fully connected layers for both its encoder and decoder [Figure 1, 3.1].\\n\\nBoth the encoder and decoder are composed of a stack of N = 6 identical layers [3.1 Encoder and Decoder Stacks].\\n\\nEach layer in the encoder has two sub-layers:\\n1. A multi-head self-attention mechanism.\\n2. A simple, position-wise fully connected feed-forward network [3.1 Encoder and Decoder Stacks].\\n\\nThe decoder also has a stack of N = 6 identical layers, which include these two sub-layers [3.1 Encoder and Decoder Stacks].\\n\\nResidual connections are employed around each of these two sub-layers, followed by layer normalization. The output of each sub-layer is LayerNorm(x+ Sublayer(x)) [We employ a residual connection]. All sub-layers and embedding layers produce outputs of dimension dmodel = 512 to facilitate these residual connections [To facilitate these residual connections].' citations=None created_at='2025-12-07T05:38:12.798366+00:00'", "id=31 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='user' content='explain the self attention mechanism' citations=None created_at='2025-12-07T05:46:20.752302+00:00'", "id=32 session_id=7 user_id=1 role='assistant' content='Self-attention, also known as intra-attention, is an attention mechanism that relates different positions of a single sequence to compute a representation of that sequence [Self-attention, sometimes called intra-attention]. It is the approach used in the model described [the approach we take in our model].\\n\\nIn a self-attention layer, all of the keys, values, and queries originate from the same place, specifically the output of the previous layer [The encoder contains self-attention layers]. An attention function, which is a core component, maps a query and a set of key-value pairs to an output. This output is calculated as a weighted sum of the values, where the weight for each value is determined by a compatibility function of the query and the corresponding key [3.2 Attention]. Self-attention layers are compared to recurrent and convolutional layers for mapping variable-length sequences of symbol representations [4 Why Self-Attention].' citations=None created_at='2025-12-07T05:46:30.807351+00:00'"]
